{"files":[{"content":"#include \"knn.h\"\n\ntypedef struct {\n    size_t encounter;\n    float distance;\n    char label;\n} Candidate;\n\nstatic int candidate_is_worse(const Candidate *a, const Candidate *b) {\n    if (a->distance > b->distance) return 1;\n    if (a->distance < b->distance) return 0;\n    return a->encounter > b->encounter;\n}\n\nstatic void swap_candidates(Candidate *a, Candidate *b) {\n    Candidate temporary = *a;\n    *a = *b;\n    *b = temporary;\n}\n\nstatic void heap_sift_up(Candidate *heap, size_t child) {\n    while (child > 0) {\n        size_t parent = (child - 1) / 2;\n        if (!candidate_is_worse(&heap[child], &heap[parent])) break;\n        swap_candidates(&heap[child], &heap[parent]);\n        child = parent;\n    }\n}\n\nstatic void heap_sift_down(Candidate *heap, size_t heap_size, size_t root) {\n    while (root < heap_size / 2) {\n        size_t worse_child = root * 2 + 1;\n        size_t right_child = worse_child + 1;\n        if (right_child < heap_size &&\n            candidate_is_worse(&heap[right_child], &heap[worse_child])) {\n            worse_child = right_child;\n        }\n        if (!candidate_is_worse(&heap[worse_child], &heap[root])) break;\n        swap_candidates(&heap[worse_child], &heap[root]);\n        root = worse_child;\n    }\n}\n\nchar knn(int n_groups, Group *groups, int k, Point to_evaluate) {\n    size_t capacity = (size_t)k;\n    Candidate *heap = (Candidate *)malloc(sizeof(Candidate) * capacity);\n    char *labels = (char *)malloc(sizeof(char) * capacity);\n    size_t heap_size = 0;\n    size_t encounter = 0;\n\n    for (size_t i = 0; i < capacity; ++i) {\n        labels[i] = -1;\n    }\n\n    const float query_x = to_evaluate.x;\n    const float query_y = to_evaluate.y;\n\n    for (int i = 0; i < n_groups; ++i) {\n        const Group *group = &groups[i];\n        const float *x_coordinates = group->x_coordinates;\n        const float *y_coordinates = group->y_coordinates;\n        char label = group->label;\n\n        for (int j = 0; j < group->length; ++j) {\n            float dx = x_coordinates[j] - query_x;\n            float dy = y_coordinates[j] - query_y;\n            float distance = dx * dx + dy * dy;\n            Candidate candidate = { encounter, distance, label };\n\n            if (heap_size < capacity) {\n                size_t position = heap_size++;\n                heap[position] = candidate;\n                heap_sift_up(heap, position);\n            } else if (candidate_is_worse(&heap[0], &candidate)) {\n                heap[0] = candidate;\n                heap_sift_down(heap, heap_size, 0);\n            }\n\n            ++encounter;\n        }\n    }\n\n    for (size_t i = 0; i < heap_size; ++i) {\n        labels[i] = heap[i].label;\n    }\n\n    qsort(labels, capacity, sizeof(char), compare_for_sort);\n\n    char most_frequent = labels[0];\n    int most_frequent_count = 1;\n    int current_frequency = 1;\n\n    for (int i = 1; i < k; i++) {\n        if (labels[i] != labels[i - 1]) {\n            if (current_frequency > most_frequent_count) {\n                most_frequent = labels[i - 1];\n                most_frequent_count = current_frequency;\n            }\n\n            current_frequency = 1;\n        } else {\n            current_frequency++;\n        }\n\n        if (i == k - 1 && current_frequency > most_frequent_count) {\n            most_frequent = labels[i - 1];\n            most_frequent_count = current_frequency;\n        }\n    }\n\n    free(heap);\n    free(labels);\n    return most_frequent;\n}\n\nint main() {\n    int n_groups = parse_number_of_groups();\n    Group *groups = (Group *)malloc(sizeof(Group) * n_groups);\n\n    for (int i = 0; i < n_groups; i++) {\n        groups[i] = parse_next_group();\n    }\n\n    int k = parse_k();\n    Point to_evaluate = parse_point();\n\n    printf(\"%c\", knn(n_groups, groups, k, to_evaluate));\n}\n","path":"src/knn.c"},{"content":"#include <stdio.h>\n#include <stdlib.h>\n\ntypedef struct {\n    float x;\n    float y;\n} Point;\n\ntypedef struct {\n    char label;\n    int length;\n    float *x_coordinates;\n    float *y_coordinates;\n} Group;\n\nvoid on_error() {\n    printf(\"Invalid input file.\\n\");\n    exit(1);\n}\n\nint parse_number_of_groups() {\n    int n;\n    if (scanf(\" n_groups=%d \", &n) != 1) on_error();\n\n    return n;\n}\n\nPoint parse_point() {\n    float x, y;\n    if (scanf(\" (%f ,%f) \", &x, &y) != 2) on_error();\n\n    Point point;\n    point.x = x;\n    point.y = y;\n\n    return point;\n}\n\nGroup parse_next_group() {\n    char label;\n    int length;\n\n    if (scanf(\" label=%c \", &label) != 1) on_error();\n    if (scanf(\" length=%d \", &length) != 1) on_error();\n\n    Group group;\n    group.label = label;\n    group.length = length;\n\n    size_t point_count = (size_t)length;\n    size_t storage_count = point_count == 0 ? 1 : 2 * point_count;\n    float *coordinate_storage = (float *)malloc(sizeof(float) * storage_count);\n    group.x_coordinates = coordinate_storage;\n    group.y_coordinates = coordinate_storage + point_count;\n\n    for (int i = 0; i < length; i++) {\n        Point point = parse_point();\n        group.x_coordinates[i] = point.x;\n        group.y_coordinates[i] = point.y;\n    }\n\n    return group;\n}\n\nint parse_k() {\n    int k;\n    if (scanf(\" k=%d \", &k) != 1) on_error();\n\n    return k;\n}\n\nfloat euclidean_distance_no_sqrt(Point a, Point b) {\n    return ((b.x - a.x) * ((b.x - a.x))) + ((b.y - a.y) * (b.y - a.y));\n}\n\nint compare_for_sort(const void *a, const void *b) {\n    return *(char *)a - *(char *)b;\n}\n","path":"src/knn.h"}],"hypothesis":"Storing each group in contiguous x and y coordinate planes should make the point scan more cache-friendly than interleaved Point records. A bounded max-heap keeps candidate storage O(k) and uses encounter order to preserve stable distance-tie selection.","notes":"The controller should evaluate exact output and performance; no measurements were run here.","sources_kept":[],"transformations":["Changed each group's point storage from interleaved Point records to x/y structure-of-arrays planes in one allocation, filled during parsing.","Scanned the coordinate planes sequentially and hoisted query coordinates out of the point loop.","Used a max-heap ordered by squared distance and original encounter index, then retained the existing label sort and vote logic."]}